Manual integration reference; not a directly applicable patch.

Key changes for apps/kimi-shell/src-tauri/src/context_menu.rs:

- Remove AllFilesystemObjects from the set of keys written and validated:

- const ALL_FS_SHELL_KEY: &str = r"Software\Classes\AllFilesystemObjects\shell\KimiWebShell";
- const ALL_FS_COMMAND_KEY: &str = r"Software\Classes\AllFilesystemObjects\shell\KimiWebShell\command";
- const ALL_FS_MOVE_PARENT_KEY: &str = r"Software\Classes\AllFilesystemObjects\shell\MoveToWorkspace";
- const ALL_FS_MOVE_DEFAULT_SHELL_KEY: ...
- const ALL_FS_MOVE_DEFAULT_COMMAND_KEY: ...
- const ALL_FS_MOVE_PICKER_SHELL_KEY: ...
- const ALL_FS_MOVE_PICKER_COMMAND_KEY: ...

- Keep the old top-level keys only in an explicit cleanup list so an upgrade
  removes stale registrations created by previous versions:

+ const LEGACY_OVERLAPPING_KEYS: &[&str] = &[
+     r"Software\Classes\AllFilesystemObjects\shell\KimiWebShell",
+     r"Software\Classes\AllFilesystemObjects\shell\MoveToWorkspace",
+ ];
+
+ fn cleanup_legacy_overlapping_keys(hkcu: &RegKey) -> Result<(), String> {
+     for key in LEGACY_OVERLAPPING_KEYS {
+         delete_key_if_exists(hkcu, key)?;
+     }
+     Ok(())
+ }

- The desired registrations become:

  Directory\Background\shell\KimiWebShell -> --open-dir -- "%V"
  Directory\shell\KimiWebShell            -> --open-dir -- "%1"
  *\shell\KimiWebShell                    -> --open-files -- "%1"
  Directory\shell\MoveToWorkspace         -> copy submenu
  *\shell\MoveToWorkspace                 -> copy submenu

- Call cleanup_legacy_overlapping_keys during enable, disable and migration,
  then call SHChangeNotify once after the complete operation.

Key changes for apps/kimi-shell/src-tauri/src/settings_store.rs:

+ if settings.schema_version < 10 {
